{"obsah":"<p><strong>23/8 – </strong><strong>Hovězí+ festival exhibition – charity exhibition in Velešín</strong></p>\n\n<p>Light rain before the show didn't stop us, and Vlasta and Tobík performed our classic show at the local festival combined with a contest for the best goulash. The beef one won, of course, and the guys got to taste it. Thanks for the invitation.</p>\n\n<p><strong>30/8 – </strong><strong>Exhibition in Valdice&nbsp;</strong></p>\n\n<p>Luckily we didn't have to go and sit in the local prison – we just had to celebrate the local festival with concerts in a nearby park. The line-up of Vlasta and Michal Budský was unexpectedly joined by our friend Hannes Hermann (multiple German champion), so the locals got to see a truly first-class Trial show.</p>\n\n<p><strong>5/9 – Road trade fair in Pardubice</strong></p>\n\n<p>Once again we were invited to Pardubice for the traditional road trade fair focused on technology and projects related to roads and related services. The exhibition took place by the main stage and was also shown on LED screens around the grounds. Martin Šimůnek and Vlasta had about 20 minutes to demonstrate their sporting art.</p>\n\n<p><strong>6/9 – Triple exhibition in Stonařov, Vraňany and Choceň</strong></p>\n\n<p>Martin Šimůnek and Michal Budský headed to a sports day in Choceň, where they entertained athletes and spectators in 3 short shows. At the same time Vlasta and Lukáš Valný set off for Stonařov for a farewell to summer with a fairly decent turnout. After the show they had to quickly pack the obstacles and bikes and head to Vraňany for the local fair. All exhibitions done – this time Martin and Michal won on number of shows, but Vlasta and Lukáš won on kilometres. Thanks to all the organisers for the invitations.</p>\n\n<p><strong>13/9 – Double exhibition in Říčany and Kunratice</strong></p>\n\n<p>This time we rode on our doorstep. For our home club, together with the club's little ones, we rode a show with 8 riders on the Lázeňská louka meadow in Říčany, where leisure activities and clubs were being presented. We spent some time on the meadow, greeted all our friends and fans, and after training with the kids, Tobík Dolák and Lukáš Valný headed to nearby Kunratice, where a children's day organised by the local theatre took place in the beautiful setting of the chateau park. By the main stage we rode an exhibition, also using the stage, and although it didn't look like it at first, with a decent crowd. The show was originally supposed to be ridden by Martin Šimůnek, who injured his back – we wish him a speedy recovery. Thanks for the invitation.</p>\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-gallery has-nested-images columns-default is-cropped\">\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><a href=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/bikeskills-web.firebasestorage.app/o/wp-content%2Fuploads%2F2025%2F09%2FIMG_1608.webp?alt=media\"><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/bikeskills-web.firebasestorage.app/o/wp-content%2Fuploads%2F2025%2F09%2FIMG_1608.webp?alt=media\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-251043\"/></a></figure>\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><a href=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/bikeskills-web.firebasestorage.app/o/wp-content%2Fuploads%2F2025%2F09%2Fimage-77.webp?alt=media\"><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/bikeskills-web.firebasestorage.app/o/wp-content%2Fuploads%2F2025%2F09%2Fimage-77.webp?alt=media\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-251039\"/></a></figure>\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><a href=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/bikeskills-web.firebasestorage.app/o/wp-content%2Fuploads%2F2025%2F09%2F20250906_114042.webp?alt=media\"><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/bikeskills-web.firebasestorage.app/o/wp-content%2Fuploads%2F2025%2F09%2F20250906_114042.webp?alt=media\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-251042\"/></a></figure>\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><a href=\"https